Ladybird now removes a line’s trailing collapsible spaces before
aligning it, whichever direction the line is and whatever ends
it. Gecko’s nsBlockFrame::PlaceLine() calls nsLineLayout::
TrimTrailingWhiteSpace() before nsLineLayout::TextAlignLine(),
Blink’s LineBreaker::RemoveTrailingCollapsibleSpace() runs before
InlineLayoutAlgorithm::ApplyTextAlign(), and WebKit’s line builder
calls Line::handleTrailingTrimmableContent() before the line is aligned.
Checked in Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5: All
three put the line before the br at the right edge, and center it on the
same axis as the lines around it.
